---
description: Python conventions for the scout package
globs: scout/**/*.py, tests/**/*.py, scripts/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- Python 3.10+, type hints on all public functions, pydantic v2 models for data crossing a boundary.
- Pydantic models use `ConfigDict(extra="forbid")`.
- Functions take their dependencies (for example the LLM client) as arguments so tests can inject fakes.
  No network calls at import time.
- Raise specific exceptions (`GuardrailError`, `ValueError`), never bare `Exception`.
- Keep modules under 150 lines. No new dependencies beyond pyproject.toml without a note in the PR.
